- venue: bioRxiv
- citation count: 0
[method]
The paper used an all-optical two-photon approach in mouse visual cortex, combining in vivo two-photon calcium imaging with in vivo two-photon holographic photostimulation to monitor and manipulate neuronal activity at single-cell resolution. A bicistronic construct expressing jGCaMP8s and stChrimsonR was used to enable simultaneous calcium imaging and optogenetic stimulation. The workflow included virus injection and surgery, widefield fluorescence imaging to assess expression, retinotopic mapping, visual stimulation, two-photon calcium imaging analysis, visual tuning analysis, and measurement of the half-decay time of photostimulation responses. This is directly related to the proposed research method, which also uses an all-optical two-photon strategy combining GCaMP8s calcium imaging with holographic optogenetic stimulation to manipulate small ensembles while monitoring network responses in awake mice.
[results]
The supplied paper excerpt contains only section headings and does not provide numerical results. The headings indicate that the bicistronic construct produced robust expression of jGCaMP8s and stChrimsonR; visually evoked and spontaneous activity could be recorded from V1 cells expressing the construct; visual responses were stable over time; and cells showed robust and stable responses to both optogenetic and visual stimulation. No quantitative response amplitudes, tuning indices, session-to-session correlations, half-decay time values, p-values, or control comparisons are available from the provided text.
[context]
The paper context is visual cortex rather than auditory cortex, so the sensory stimulus is visual rather than 16 kHz or 54 kHz tones, and the tuning analysis is visual rather than frequency tuning. The provided excerpt does not specify animal numbers, imaging wavelengths, laser powers, hologram parameters, stimulation duration, session number, or statistical thresholds. The relevant context for the proposed plan is that the paper validates the core all-optical two-photon imaging plus holographic photostimulation pipeline, including a bicistronic calcium indicator/opsin construct, retinotopic targeting, visual evoked response stability, and optogenetic response kinetics. This supports the feasibility of the proposed four-session auditory ensemble manipulation paradigm, especially the use of a co-expressed fast calcium indicator and red-shifted opsin, the need to assess stability across sessions, and the measurement of temporal dynamics of optogenetically evoked responses.
[end related work 1]

