    "suggested_action": "Most important, replace a simple one-dimensional distance-decay control with a spatially explicit ORF mapping protocol modeled on [(Triplett et al., 2023-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/9d1fdb72be2328293d106365d9f20374230ad1a3): for each of the five target cells, shift the 15 μm spiral hologram on an x/y grid, for example -20 to +20 μm in 5-10 μm steps, and if feasible add z offsets of -30 to +30 μm, at 5 mW per cell and at lower powers, record GCaMP8s ΔF/F, fit a GP-Bernoulli or equivalent activation-probability model, and use the fitted field to reposition holograms and adjust power to minimize off-target activation while preserving target activation. Second, calibrate and control the illumination field as emphasized by [(Ronzitti et al., 2017-10)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/20b6db4822512484b3fda84d998d801e21196604): measure the actual PSF and speckle statistics of the 15 μm spiral at the target plane, use speckle-free CGH or time averaging, fill the pupil to preserve NA, and include 0 mW and shifted-pattern controls to separate biological response decay from illumination artifacts. Third, quantify multi-cell stimulation reliability by reporting per-cell activation probability, write-in error, and trial-to-trial variability across the five-cell ensemble, with confidence intervals and significance tests, rather than only mean response amplitude. Fourth, if axial control is available, test depth-dependent decay using multi-plane CGH or defocused holograms, because both [(Triplett et al., 2023-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/9d1fdb72be2328293d106365d9f20374230ad1a3) and [(Ronzitti et al., 2017-10)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/20b6db4822512484b3fda84d998d801e21196604) show that depth is a major determinant of off-target activation. Finally, match stimulation parameters to rsChRmine kinetics by testing shorter durations and power ramps around the planned 100 ms, 5 mW per cell condition to avoid saturation and ensure that the distance-decay measurement is not limited by opsin kinetics or calcium indicator dynamics.",
